 ## Background
-The method is attributed to Inigo Quilez, a prominent graphics programmer known for his work on ray marching and SDFs [S1, unofficial]. It is widely known in the procedural geometry community as "Quilez smin" [S2, unofficial]. The technique is used in real-time ray marching shaders for creating complex organic shapes from simple primitives [S3, unofficial].
